# asr61_dipole.g4bl -- muE4 ASR61 dipole, ISOLATED, for comparison against OPALX.
#
# The same 13 muons (beam.txt, written by make_parts.py) go through the same
# G4beamline `grid` field map here and in asr61_dipole.in, and the two outputs
# are compared particle by particle.
#
# Nothing but the dipole field can cause a difference: vacuum world, no iron
# housing, no decay, no stochastic processes.
#
# FRAME: z here [mm] / 1000 == path length s in asr61_dipole.in [m].
#   The map's own z runs -1380..+1380 mm, so placing it at z=1500 puts the field
#   at z = 120..2880 mm.  OPALX gets ELEMEDGE = 1.500, which is where the map's
#   z=0 lands, and sees the same span.
#
#   The centerline is STRAIGHT here, unlike mue4_WsxOn.g4bl, which wraps this
#   magnet in two `cornerarc` commands so the centerline follows the beam. A
#   straight centerline is what makes the comparison one to one: OPALX's SBEND
#   carries ANGLE = 0 for the same reason. The orbit leaves the map sideways
#   near x = 390 mm, which is where the map's own box ends, in both codes.
#
# Run from this directory:
#   source /Users/rammann/Code/G4BL/G4beamline-3.08.app/Contents/root/bin/thisroot.sh
#   g4bl asr61_dipole.g4bl

physics QGSP_BERT disable=Decay doStochastics=0

param worldMaterial=Vacuum

# Tracking accuracy. NOTE the capital S in maxStep -- `maxstep` is a different,
# unused parameter.
param maxStep=1.0 deltaChord=0.01

# `start` must come before every `place` -- it aborts with "Invalid start" if a
# centerline segment already exists.
start x=0 y=0 z=0 initialZ=0 radiusCut=2000
reference particle=mu+ referenceMomentum=28
trackcuts keep=mu+ killSecondaries=1

# The shared particle set. renumber=0 (the default) means EventID is taken from
# the file, so EventID == OPALX id + 1.  Do NOT set beamZ: it forces z=0 on
# every particle and would wipe out any longitudinal offsets.
beam ascii filename=beam.txt

# `fieldmap` places no physical volume, so nothing would expand the world and
# every track would leave immediately. This vacuum box is the world envelope.
# It has to be wide enough in x for the bent orbit, which reaches x = 1.25 m.
box WORLDBOX height=1000 width=4000 length=4200 material=Vacuum
place WORLDBOX z=1500 x=1000

# The element under test. current= is the deck-side multiplier on the tabulated
# Tesla; OPALX spells it FMAPSCALE.
fieldmap MAG file=../../../../g4bl-files/muE4/maps/asr61_300d_track.g4blmap current=-9.9528E-01
place MAG z=1500

# Recording planes, in field-free drift 70 mm outside the map.
# zntuple interpolates each track linearly onto the exact plane -- the same
# construction an OPALX MONITOR uses.  format=ascii writes a #BLTrackFile, so
# the comparison needs no ROOT.  Files are named after the plane: Z50.txt,
# Z2950.txt.  There is no `corner` in this file, so centerline == global.
zntuple z=50,2950 format=ascii coordinates=centerline

# On-axis field, no tracking involved -- the field-import check. The orbit does
# not stay on the axis, but the axis samples are what both codes must agree on
# before any tracking difference means anything.
fieldntuple AXIS format=ascii filename=g4bl_axis.txt x=0 y=0 z=150,2850,5 t=0
